---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SOURCE_URL } from "../data/site";
import { manifest } from "../data/screenshots";

const app = [
  {
    name: "MediaPipe Tasks Vision, including its WebAssembly runtime",
    detail: "@mediapipe/tasks-vision 0.10.35, by Google",
    license: "Apache License 2.0",
  },
  {
    name: "MediaPipe Face Landmarker model",
    detail: "face_landmarker.task, float16, version 1, by Google",
    license: "Apache License 2.0",
  },
  {
    name: "RealEye's open-source eye-image model",
    detail: "Reads where you look from small eye images, on the device",
    license: "See THIRD_PARTY.md",
  },
  {
    name: "Synapse-Mesh and the AGENCY desktop design",
    detail:
      "By Ray: the request router with its Cisco network sentinel, and the macOS-style desktop interface",
    license: "Part of this project",
  },
  {
    name: "QR Code Generator for JavaScript",
    detail: "qrcode-generator 1.4.4, by Kazuhiko Arase",
    license: "MIT License",
  },
  {
    name: "Atkinson Hyperlegible",
    detail: "Typeface by the Braille Institute of America, packaged by Fontsource",
    license: "SIL Open Font License 1.1",
  },
  {
    name: "React, Vite, FastAPI, Pydantic, Uvicorn, the Google Gen AI SDK and other dependencies",
    detail: "Listed in the project's package.json and backend requirements files",
    license: "Their own open-source licenses",
  },
];

const site = [
  { name: "Astro", detail: "The tool that builds this site into plain HTML", license: "MIT License" },
  {
    name: "Atkinson Hyperlegible",
    detail: "@fontsource/atkinson-hyperlegible 5.3.0, served from this site",
    license: "SIL Open Font License 1.1",
  },
  { name: "sharp", detail: "Image resizing at build time", license: "Apache License 2.0" },
  {
    name: "Playwright, axe-core, Lighthouse CI, Vitest, TypeScript, Prettier",
    detail: "Testing and checking tools, used only when building; none of them run in your browser",
    license: "Apache License 2.0, MPL 2.0 (axe-core) and MIT",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Credits and licenses: AGENCY OS"
  description="The open-source work AGENCY OS and this website are built on, and their licenses."
  current="credits"
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Credits and licenses</p>
    <h1>Built on the work of others</h1>
    <p class="lede">AGENCY OS and this site use these components. Thank you to everyone who made them.</p>

    <h2 id="app">In the AGENCY app</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Components in the AGENCY app" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Component</th>
            <th scope="col">Details</th>
            <th scope="col">License</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {app.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{c.name}</th>
              <td>{c.detail}</td>
              <td>{c.license}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The authoritative list, with versions and checksums, is{" "}
      <a href={`${SOURCE_URL}/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY.md`}>THIRD_PARTY.md</a> in the repository. It grows as
      AGENCY OS adds parts such as the Mac app shell and the Chrome extension.
    </p>

    <h2 id="site">In this website</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Components in this website" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Component</th>
            <th scope="col">Details</th>
            <th scope="col">License</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{c.name}</th>
              <td>{c.detail}</td>
              <td>{c.license}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="screenshots">Screenshots</h2>
    <p>
      Every screenshot on this site is a real capture of the AGENCY app, taken automatically by a script in
      the repository (<code>site/scripts/capture-screenshots.mjs</code>) on {manifest.captured} from commit
      <code>{manifest.commit}</code>, using fictional demo data (“Jordan”, “Thai Basil” and practice services)
      and the built-in demo agent. None are mock-ups. The eye-scan and network-mode pictures on the home page
      are drawings, not screenshots.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Bartlett G, Blais R, Tamblyn R, Clermont RJ, MacGibbon B.{" "}
        <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2396356">
          Impact of patient communication problems on the risk of preventable adverse events in acute care
          settings
        </a>
        . CMAJ 2008;178(12):1555–62.
      </li>
      <li>
        Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC): about 33,000 people in the United States live with
        ALS.
      </li>
      <li>
        Beukelman D, Fager S, Nordness A. Communication support for people with ALS. Neurology Research
        International, 2011: 80 to 95% of people with ALS become unable to rely on natural speech.
      </li>
      <li>
        Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services (CMS), 2026 DMEPOS fee schedule: about $9,646 for a
        speech-generating device.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="project">AGENCY itself</h2>
    <p>
      AGENCY began at the UCSC AI Hackathon and is built in the open on <a href={SOURCE_URL}>GitHub</a>. The
      project hasn't chosen a license for its own code yet; until it does, the code can be read but no license
      to reuse it is granted.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
